# Build context excludes for console/Dockerfile.
#
# Rule of thumb: exclude anything that is (a) regenerated inside the build,
# (b) host-specific, or (c) a secret. Test sources are deliberately NOT
# excluded — tsconfig.json globs them, and `next build` runs tsc, so dropping
# them from the context can change type-checking behaviour.

# Regenerated inside the image by `bun install` / `bun run build`.
node_modules
.next
out

# Host-only build + test artefacts.
playwright-report
test-results
coverage
# Incremental tsc state recorded against macOS host paths. Shipping it into the
# build can make `next build` skip type-checking files it should re-check.
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

.git

# Secrets: never baked into a layer. The console is configured at runtime, so
# no .env file is needed at build time. REVERSE (narrow this to `.env*.local`)
# only if the app ever needs a build-time NEXT_PUBLIC_* value, and even then
# prefer a --build-arg over a committed file.
.env*

# Editor / OS noise.
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
*.log

*.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
